---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="GibTalk doesn't collect or store any of your data."
>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: 29 September 2026</p>

  <p>
    GibTalk doesn't collect or store any of your data, or track how you use it.
    There's no account, no login, no analytics, no advertising, and no cookies
    or unique identifiers.
  </p>

  <h2>Your words and pictures</h2>
  <p>
    Everything you add stays on your device: your words, their pictures and any
    photos you take. GibTalk works offline. Nothing is uploaded.
  </p>
  <p>
    Backups are files saved on your device. Where they go after that is up to
    you.
  </p>

  <h2>When GibTalk goes online</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Searching symbols</strong> sends your search words to the GibTalk
      symbols server (<code>api-gibtalk.apps.bancuh.net</code>, also reachable
      as <code>api.gibtalk.ragib.my</code>) and downloads the matching pictures.
      Searches aren't linked to you, and there's no account to link them to.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Templates</strong> are downloaded from GibTalk's public GitHub
      repository when you open the Templates screen. Their pictures come from
      the same symbols server.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Speaking words</strong> uses your device's built-in
      text-to-speech.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    As with any website, those servers can see your IP address when your device
    downloads from them.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    gibtalk.ragib.dev has no analytics and no cookies. The symbol search on this
    site sends your search words to the same symbols server.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the new version will be posted here, with a new date
    at the top.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions? <a href={SITE.issues}>Open an issue on GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
